l hours — check the official site"},"summary":"Patna Museum is the state museum of the Indian state of Bihar. Founded on 3 April 1917 during the British Raj to house the historical artefacts found in the vicinity of Patna, it is constructed in the style of Mughal and Rajput architecture, and is known locally as the Jadu Ghar.","summarySource":"wikipedia","wikipediaTitle":"Patna Museum","names":{"ja":"パトナ博物館"},"photo":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Patnamuseum1.JPG/1280px-Patnamuseum1.JPG","thumb":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Patnamuseum1.JPG/500px-Patnamuseum1.JPG","w":1200,"h":900,"author":"Manoj nav at English Wikipedia","license":"Public domain","licenseUrl":"","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Patnamuseum1.JPG"}},{"id":"patna_buddha_smriti_park","areaId":"patna","name":"Buddha Smriti Park","category":"park","tags":["nature","photo"],"location":{"lat":25.60667,"lng":85.13611},"visitMinutes":60,"priceLevel":0,"photoSeed":"patna_buddha_smriti_park","tickets":[{"vendor":"Official","url":"https://web.archive.org/web/20130806022031/http://buddha-smriti-park.com","official":true}],"signals":{"commonsDepicts":0,"commonsNearby":5,"wikiPageviews":360,"wikidataSitelinks":6,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-21"},"hashtags":["buddhasmritipark","patna"],"bestLight":"golden","summary":"Buddha Smriti Park is also known as Buddha Memorial Park is an urban park located on Frazer Road near Patna Junction in Patna, India. This park has been designed by Vikram Lall and developed by the Bihar Government to commemorate the 2554th birth anniversary of the Buddha.","summarySource":"wikipedia","wikipediaTitle":"Buddha Smriti Park","photo":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/06/Budhha-Memorial-Park-Patna.jpg/1280px-Budhha-Memorial-Park-Patna.jpg","thumb":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/06/Budhha-Memorial-Park-Patna.jpg/500px-Budhha-Memorial-Park-Patna.jpg","w":1200,"h":1085,"au